WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:01.130
Moutstache Bob Stokey, walking along like
he’s in a cormac mccarthy novel.

00:00:01.130 --> 00:00:02.130
Making himself a drunk hut.

00:00:02.130 --> 00:00:03.130
Almost like he’s making himself a prison.

00:00:03.130 --> 00:00:04.130
The montage has a nice song on it.

00:00:04.130 --> 00:00:05.130
Why is he by himself though?

00:00:05.130 --> 00:00:06.130
Daryl pulls up on a bike with Glenn.

00:00:06.130 --> 00:00:07.130
This must be a flashback to when Bob first
found them.

00:00:07.130 --> 00:00:08.130
Daryl asks him the three questions.

00:00:08.130 --> 00:00:09.130
“It doesn’t matter who you are.”

00:00:09.130 --> 00:00:10.130
Flash forward to the mist, bob, sasha, maggie.

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:11.130
Walkers sounds all around.

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:12.130
massing - best moment.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:13.130
(smoke machine joke).

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:14.130
Maggie almost goes down just like beth.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.130
Bob gets bit and seems like he’s lying about
it.

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:16.130
Daryl still teaching Beth to track, she’s
having fun now.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:17.130
She’s turning into Arya Stark.

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.130
She steps on a trap and almost gets bit.

00:00:18.130 --> 00:00:19.130
“Pretty soon I won’t need you anymore”.

00:00:19.130 --> 00:00:20.130
Moment is good example of why she still does.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:21.130
Maggie’s compass broken and fog everywhere.

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:22.130
They’re lost.

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:23.130
Daryl gives beth Piggy back ride.

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:24.130
They find another house.

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:25.130
They stop to put flowers on a grave.

00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:26.130
“I don’t think the good ones survive”.

00:00:26.130 --> 00:00:27.130
The grave was a father, makes her think about
Hershel.

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:28.130
Maggie etc find train tracks and Sanctuary
sign.

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.130
Terminus.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:30.130
Bob stokey references the time in the car
they heard the message.

00:00:30.130 --> 00:00:31.130
Sasha is mistrusful.

00:00:31.130 --> 00:00:32.130
Daryl and beth find out it’s a funeral parlor.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.130
Walker looks like it was prepped.

00:00:33.130 --> 00:00:34.130
Beth wants to leave thank you note, daryl
suggests staying.

00:00:34.130 --> 00:00:35.130
He’s getting nicer, Beth is rubbing off
on him.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:36.130
She makes fun of his shrugging emotes.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.130
They have a very awkward pause.

00:00:37.130 --> 00:00:38.130
Walkers mass.

00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:39.130
Daryl barely escapes.

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:40.130
The show is teasing us with dead or dying
characters.

00:00:40.130 --> 00:00:41.130
Beth takes off in a car.

00:00:41.130 --> 00:00:42.130
Whole lotta bob stokey and sasha.

00:00:42.130 --> 00:00:43.130
He’s still bleeding from his wound.

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:44.130
They’re trying to catch maggie, who has
been leaving messages for Glenn using walker

00:00:44.130 --> 00:00:45.130
blood.

00:00:45.130 --> 00:00:46.130
Bob stokey sasha kiss doesn’t seem super
romantic.

00:00:46.130 --> 00:00:47.130
She tells him “You don’t have to be alone
again.”

00:00:47.130 --> 00:00:48.130
Bob is being really noble but he’s probably
going to die.

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:49.130
She finds maggie lying in a pile of bodies
after stokey takes off.

00:00:49.130 --> 00:00:50.130
Daryl is running down the road.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:51.130
Looks like he needs some exercise.

00:00:51.130 --> 00:00:52.130
He finds the railroad tracks too.

00:00:52.130 --> 00:00:53.130
Maggie finally calms the fuck down and asks
sasha for help and they head after bob stokey

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.130
and plan to head toward terminus.

00:00:54.130 --> 00:00:55.130
Daryl sits down in a pile near the tracks
and runs into the people that found Rick.

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:56.130
They circle him and looks like he’s going
to die.

00:00:56.130 --> 00:00:57.130
“Why hurt yourself when you can hurt other
people.”

00:00:57.130 --> 00:00:58.130
- tells him his name’s joe.

00:00:58.130 --> 00:00:59.130
Seems like they’re not going to kill him
then.

00:00:59.130 --> 00:01:00.130
Bob back on his own again like in the beginning,
but maggie and beth find him.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:01.130
and it seems all good.

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:02.130
Glenn touches terminus sign so seems like
everyone but rick’s group meeting up.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:03.130
Back to carol’s group next.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:04.130
Looks like the girls are in trouble.

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:05.130
Where did beth go?

00:01:05.130 --> 00:01:06.130
What’s going to happen to bob.

00:01:06.130 --> 00:01:07.130
Hey youtubers it’s charlie and this week
on Walking Dead death was just hanging over

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:08.130
everyone like a cloud.

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.130
The episode title was Alone and there were
a lot of teasers for Sanctuary as has been

00:01:09.130 --> 00:01:10.130
the tradition since the show came back and
potential reunions.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:11.130
There were also a few things that made me
re-evaluate who I think is going to end up

00:01:11.130 --> 00:01:12.130
dying.

00:01:12.130 --> 00:01:13.130
Quick shoutout to the Giveaway this week.

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:14.130
If you’re finding me for the first time
I just give away a gift card for each episode

00:01:14.130 --> 00:01:15.130
of Walking Dead to say thank you to you guys
for being so awesome.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:16.130
All you have to do to enter is be a subscriber
and leave a comment on this video.

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:17.130
I’ll be announcing the winner in my Q&amp;A
video tomorrow.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:18.130
So now let’s talk about our Top 5 WTF Moments
and then I’ll do my review.

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:19.130
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
the episode yet.

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:20.130
Number 5 - Maggie Takes off looking for Glenn.

00:01:20.130 --> 00:01:21.130
So as the title implies there was going to
be some separating in the episode and Maggie

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:22.130
and Beth had this weird sister mojo between
them where for some reason they were both

00:01:22.130 --> 00:01:23.130
the ones to lose it and take off running.

00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:24.130
Maggie of course not being one to waste resources
totally used the walkers as finger paints.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:25.130
I have to say this wasn’t the biggest plot
point, but I laughed and threw up in my mouth

00:01:25.130 --> 00:01:26.130
at the same time.

00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:27.130
Maggie is so crazy, so much more crazy than
I think we realize.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:28.130
Sasha had that great monologue where she talked
about getting warnings and only getting them

00:01:28.130 --> 00:01:29.130
once.

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:30.130
Maggie kind of got hers, and even though she
realized she needed help I wonder what’s

00:01:30.130 --> 00:01:31.130
going to happen in the next situation like
this.

00:01:31.130 --> 00:01:32.130
I have a feeling Sasha won’t magically appear
to rescue her.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.219
Number 4 - Beth Leaves Daryl in the dust.

00:01:34.219 --> 00:01:38.700
WTF, this was one of my bigger fist shaking
moments.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:42.860
We didn’t see her get in the car, but it’s
implied that she’s the one that took off.

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:46.340
Daryl on the other hand had that thing that
the governor had, where no matter how many

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:50.560
Walkers pile on you, they always crawl away
without a scratch.

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:57.060
Daryl isn’t invincible, but I’m sure the
theory will get tested even more.

00:01:57.060 --> 00:01:59.790
Number 3 - Beth starts turning into Arya Stark.

00:01:59.790 --> 00:02:04.420
I loved the opening scene with them so much,
but I always get frustrated when characters

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:07.810
that are clearly smart have slip and falls.

00:02:07.810 --> 00:02:10.760
That’s what I’m calling Beth stepping
in the trap.

00:02:10.760 --> 00:02:15.400
It’s like she can learn Daryl’s complex
bow but she can’t walk without falling down.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:19.230
I blame the writers for things like that,
they’re trying to show us how Beth thinks

00:02:19.230 --> 00:02:21.140
she’s better than she really is.

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:25.060
But I don’t see why she has to be a klutz
for us to understand that.

00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:28.990
Putting that aside, I’ll say the big question
we need to answer is why did she tear off

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:30.240
in the car?

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:33.660
She must have either totally flipped or thought
that Daryl was dead.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:36.560
I’m choosing to believe that she just got
scared and flipped out.

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:40.620
She and Daryl had just had those long monologues
about seeing the good in everything.

00:02:40.620 --> 00:02:42.660
Even if the good ones are always destined
to die.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.100
Number 2 - Bob Stokey gets bitten.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:49.640
This could really go either way, but him getting
bit shot him to the top of my death list.

00:02:49.640 --> 00:02:53.230
He’s an alcoholic and addicts tend to lie
a lot.

00:02:53.230 --> 00:02:56.930
Mostly about drinking, but something tells
me that unless his wound gets treated in the

00:02:56.930 --> 00:03:01.040
next episode, he’s only going to get worse
and turn in the middle of the night.

00:03:01.040 --> 00:03:04.070
Hopefully he and Sasha aren’t sharing a
sleeping bag by that point.

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:07.270
The other big Bob thing that I noticed was
his Knight in shining armor routine.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:11.610
He’s probably just been doing that because
of Sasha, but I like this Bob way better than

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:14.490
the one Daryl almost threw off a roof earlier
this season.

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:17.280
We all need to keep our eyes on him though.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:23.080
Sometimes shows will build a weak character
up like this just so they can tear them down.

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:27.090
Bob just blew past Maggie on my list of people
who might die this season.

00:03:27.090 --> 00:03:29.280
and my number 1 moment.

00:03:29.280 --> 00:03:31.180
Daryl meets Joe and the psychopaths.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:34.780
I’m choosing to think of them as a version
of the Hunters from the comic book.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:38.500
We’ll have to see if they behave the same
way the comic book group does.

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.990
But Joe’s quote, why hurt yourself when
you can hurt others.

00:03:41.990 --> 00:03:44.080
Doesn’t bode well.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:46.200
This was another almost death scene.

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:48.260
Daryl just lying there in the road defeated.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:51.750
I’m so glad that it wasn’t Beth there
instead.

00:03:51.750 --> 00:03:56.780
As a bonus best moment I have to mention Glenn,
who is definitely going to see Maggie’s

00:03:56.780 --> 00:03:58.242
Finger Paint signs and find them.

00:03:58.242 --> 00:04:00.050
I love how those two think alike.

00:04:00.050 --> 00:04:03.880
Glenn is definitely stubborn, but he’s not
as crazy as Maggie.

00:04:03.880 --> 00:04:07.069
There was actually a recent fake wedding photo
of the two of them.

00:04:07.069 --> 00:04:09.780
Which kind of makes me nervous that things
won’t end well.

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:14.330
So now it’s your turn, let me know what
your favorite moment from the episode was.

00:04:14.330 --> 00:04:19.019
The three big questions we need to answer
in the comments and in my Q&amp;A tomorrow is

00:04:19.019 --> 00:04:22.690
one, where did Beth go? two, what is going
to happen to Daryl?

00:04:22.690 --> 00:04:25.050
and three, what is going to happen to Bob?

00:04:25.050 --> 00:04:28.940
Overall I gave the episode a B plus, I did
an amazing job of just hanging the threat

00:04:28.940 --> 00:04:31.370
of each person dying over our heads.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:35.720
First Maggie gets pinned, then Daryl get’s
pinned, Bob gets full on bitten.

00:04:35.720 --> 00:04:37.020
It doesn’t stop.

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:40.800
Sasha kind of has this foreboding moment as
they’re debating the Terminus and the music

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:44.560
cues make it seem like yes, The Terminus is
a bad place.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:49.310
We don’t have that much farther to go before
the finale and at the pace each group is moving

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:54.760
I wonder if that finale named “A” really
means Alexandria.

00:04:54.760 --> 00:04:57.930
Washington is not that close and if anyone
is going to get there, it’s going to take

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.389
a full tank of gas.

00:04:59.389 --> 00:05:02.670
Beth did just jump in the car, so maybe she’s
headed in that direction?

00:05:02.670 --> 00:05:06.490
Let’s discussify in the comments and be
sure to subscribe to get that Q&amp;A tomorrow.

00:05:06.490 --> 00:05:11.310
We’re probably only a week or two away from
one of the groups reaching the Terminus.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:15.889
Right now click here for that Q&amp;A and click
here for the new Game of Thrones Trailer that

00:05:15.889 --> 00:05:16.889
just posted.

00:05:16.889 --> 00:05:18.540
Thanks for watching, see you guys tomorrow.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.030
High Fives!

